The radiative corrections to the pure leptonic decay $D_s{\longrightarrow} {\ell}{{
u}}_{\ell}$ up-to one-loop order is presented. We find the virtual photon loop corrections to $D_s{\longrightarrow} {	au}{{
u}}_{	au}$ is negative and the corresponding branching ratio is larger than $3.51	imes 10^{-3}$. Considering the possible experimental resolutions, our prediction of the radiative decay $D_s{\longrightarrow} {	au}{{
u}}_{	au}\gamma$ is not so large as others, and the best radiative channel to determine the $V_{cs}$ or $f_{D_s}$ is $D_s{\longrightarrow} {\mu}{{
u}}_{\mu}{\gamma}$.

KamLAND has been used to measure the flux of $ ar{
u}_e$'s from distant nuclear reactors. In an exposure of 162 ton$\cdot$yr (145.1 days) the ratio of the number of observed inverse $ eta$-decay events to the expected number of events without disappearance is $0.611\pm 0.085 {m (stat)} \pm 0.041 {m (syst)} $ for $ ar{
u}_e$ energies $>$ 3.4 MeV. The deficit of events is inconsistent with the expected rate for standard $ ar{
u}_e$ propagation at the 99.95% confidence level. In the context of two-flavor neutrino oscillations with CPT invariance, these results exclude all oscillation solutions but the `Large Mixing Angle' solution to the solar neutrino problem using reactor $ ar{
u}_e$ sources.

We present a search for the decay $B^{+} 	o 	au^{+} 
u_{	au}$ in $88.9 	imes 10^{6}$ $\Upsilon(4S)$ decays recorded with the BABAR detector at the SLAC $B$-Factory. A sample of semi-exclusive, semi-leptonic B decays ($B^{-} 	o D^{0} \ell^{-}  ar{
u_{\ell}}X$), where $X$ is either a photon, $\pi^{0}$, or nothing, is used to identify the daughter particles that are associated with the other $B$ meson in each event. These particles are searched for evidence of a one-prong leptonic $B^{+} 	o 	au^{+} 
u_{	au}$ decay. For this data sample we set a preliminary upper limit on the branching fraction of $\mathcal{B}(B^{+} 	o 	au^{+} 
u_{	au}) < 4.9 	imes 10^{-4}$ at the 90% confidence level. This result is then combined with a statistically independent BABAR search for $B^{+} 	o 	au^{+} 
u_{	au}$ to give a combined preliminary limit of $\mathcal{B}(B^{+} 	o 	au^{+} 
u_{	au}) < 4.1 	imes 10^{-4}$.

