We report the results for nucleon decay searches via modes favored by supersymmetric grand unified models in Super-Kamiokande. Using 1489 days of full Super-Kamiokande-I data, we searched for $p 	o  ar{
u} K^+$, $n 	o  ar{
u} K^0$, $p 	o \mu^+ K^0$ and $p 	o e^+ K^0$ modes. We found no evidence for nucleon decay in any of these modes. We set lower limits of partial nucleon lifetime 2.3$	imes10^{33}$, 1.3$	imes10^{32}$, 1.3$	imes10^{33}$ and 1.0$	imes10^{33}$ years at 90% confidence level for $p 	o  ar{
u} K^+$, $n 	o  ar{
u} K^0$, $p 	o \mu^+ K^0$ and $p 	o e^+ K^0$ modes, respectively. These results give a strong constraint on supersymmetric grand unification models.

